    {
      "id": 3,
      "passage": "<p><strong>Narrator:</strong> Peter and Lynne discuss Professor Smith's article on online learning.</p><p><strong>Peter:</strong> When I read that article it was clear to me that Professor Smith does not favour the traditional methods of classroom teaching. I think it's about time to revolutionise the old teaching style, though.</p><p><strong>Lynne:</strong> I would hope that students consider the negatives of online learning before enrolling in online courses.</p><p><strong>Peter:</strong> Professor Smith points out that computer learning is well suited to some courses, especially the technical courses.</p><p><strong>Lynne:</strong> Unfortunately, that theory doesn't work for me.</p><p><strong>Peter:</strong> I think the personal interaction offered by traditional teaching is overrated in the article and doesn't have much value.</p><p><strong>Lynne:</strong> Oh, I disagree strongly, Peter.</p><p><strong>Peter:</strong> Online courses can foster students' technological skills — students will gain the technical know-how they'll need in their future endeavours.</p><p><strong>Lynne:</strong> I can't agree more.</p><p><strong>Lynne:</strong> What do you think Professor Smith means when he says online courses should be flexible in time?</p><p><strong>Peter:</strong> That's essentially the point of learning online — to allow those who can't attend courses at a fixed time.</p><p><strong>Lynne:</strong> I agree.</p><p><strong>Peter:</strong> Well, I think what he's trying to say is that students are already accustomed to doing their research on the Internet, although some people say computers could be better used for other purposes.</p><p><strong>Peter:</strong> Professor Smith probably intends to say that computers are not easily accessible and available to all students.</p><p><strong>Lynne:</strong> With online courses the student support system is already in place. Instead of asking fellow students or the professor for assistance, students would be able to get any information they need online, and this assistance would be available immediately.</p><p><strong>Lynne:</strong> I think it's all about the money — he is promoting online courses simply because he thinks it will enable the school to make more money.</p>",
      "questions": "<div class=\"section-block\" id=\"listening-part-3\">\n    <div class=\"section-head\">\n      <div class=\"num\">Questions 21–26</div>\n      <h2>Professor Smith’s article on online learning</h2>\n      <div class=\"instruction\">Who agrees with the following statements in Professor Smith’s article? Move the correct answer into the gap next to questions 21–26. <em>An answer may be used more than once.</em></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"opt-box drag-pool\" id=\"pool-pl\"><div class=\"drag-chip eh-opt\" id=\"dchip-pl-0\"><span class=\"eh-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"eh-opt-t\">Peter</span></div><div class=\"drag-chip eh-opt\" id=\"dchip-pl-1\"><span class=\"eh-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"eh-opt-t\">Lynne</span></div><div class=\"drag-chip eh-opt\" id=\"dchip-pl-2\"><span class=\"eh-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"eh-opt-t\">Both Peter and Lynne</span></div></div>\n    \n    <div class=\"drag-match-layout\">\n      <div class=\"drag-left\">\n        <div class=\"drag-col-hdr\">Statement</div>\n        <div class=\"drag-items wide-drops stmt-rows\"><div class=\"drag-item-row ielts-listening-question-item\" id=\"lq-row-21\"><strong class=\"ielts-listening-question-number\">21</strong><span class=\"drag-item-label\">It brings teaching problems when based on old methods.</span><select name=\"practice_7_21\" id=\"practice_7_21_\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 21\"><option value=\"\">Choose an answer</option><option value=\"A\">A</option><option value=\"B\">B</option><option value=\"C\">C</option></select></div><div class=\"drag-item-row ielts-listening-question-item\" id=\"lq-row-22\"><strong class=\"ielts-listening-question-number\">22</strong><span class=\"drag-item-label\">Students should be cautious about applying for an online course.</span><select name=\"practice_7_22\" id=\"practice_7_22_\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 22\"><option value=\"\">Choose an answer</option><option value=\"A\">A</option><option value=\"B\">B</option><option value=\"C\">C</option></select></div><div class=\"drag-item-row ielts-listening-question-item\" id=\"lq-row-23\"><strong class=\"ielts-listening-question-number\">23</strong><span class=\"drag-item-label\">Computers can be applied to certain courses.</span><select name=\"practice_7_23\" id=\"practice_7_23_\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 23\"><option value=\"\">Choose an answer</option><option value=\"A\">A</option><option value=\"B\">B</option><option value=\"C\">C</option></select></div><div class=\"drag-item-row ielts-listening-question-item\" id=\"lq-row-24\"><strong class=\"ielts-listening-question-number\">24</strong><span class=\"drag-item-label\">The opinion about personal contact is not helpful.</span><select name=\"practice_7_24\" id=\"practice_7_24_\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 24\"><option value=\"\">Choose an answer</option><option value=\"A\">A</option><option value=\"B\">B</option><option value=\"C\">C</option></select></div><div class=\"drag-item-row ielts-listening-question-item\" id=\"lq-row-25\"><strong class=\"ielts-listening-question-number\">25</strong><span class=\"drag-item-label\">Online courses come with technological development.</span><select name=\"practice_7_25\" id=\"practice_7_25_\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 25\"><option value=\"\">Choose an answer</option><option value=\"A\">A</option><option value=\"B\">B</option><option value=\"C\">C</option></select></div><div class=\"drag-item-row ielts-listening-question-item\" id=\"lq-row-26\"><strong class=\"ielts-listening-question-number\">26</strong><span class=\"drag-item-label\">Online courses should have more time flexibility.</span><select name=\"practice_7_26\" id=\"practice_7_26_\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 26\"><option value=\"\">Choose an answer</option><option value=\"A\">A</option><option value=\"B\">B</option><option value=\"C\">C</option></select></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"section-head\">\n      <div class=\"num\">Questions 27–30</div>\n      <div class=\"instruction\">Choose the correct letter, <em>A, B or C</em>.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-card ielts-listening-question-item\" id=\"lq-card-27\"><strong class=\"ielts-listening-question-number\">27</strong>\n    <div class=\"q-row\">\n      <span class=\"q-pill\">27</span>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What does Professor Smith think of the usage of the Internet on campus?</div>\n      \n    </div>\n    <div class=\"options\"><label class=\"option\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"practice_7_27\" value=\"A\" id=\"practice_7_27_A\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 27: A\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span>The students depend heavily on the Internet.</label><label class=\"option\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"practice_7_27\" value=\"B\" id=\"practice_7_27_B\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 27: B\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span>Schools could make better use of computers.</label><label class=\"option\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"practice_7_27\" value=\"C\" id=\"practice_7_27_C\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 27: C\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span>Teachers should encourage students to use computers.</label></div>\n  </div><div class=\"q-card ielts-listening-question-item\" id=\"lq-card-28\"><strong class=\"ielts-listening-question-number\">28</strong>\n    <div class=\"q-row\">\n      <span class=\"q-pill\">28</span>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What is the meaning of Professor Smith’s term ‘divided’?</div>\n      \n    </div>\n    <div class=\"options\"><label class=\"option\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"practice_7_28\" value=\"A\" id=\"practice_7_28_A\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 28: A\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span>Students tend to avoid using the computer.</label><label class=\"option\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"practice_7_28\" value=\"B\" id=\"practice_7_28_B\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 28: B\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span>Students don’t have access to the computer.</label><label class=\"option\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"practice_7_28\" value=\"C\" id=\"practice_7_28_C\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 28: C\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span>Students are encouraged to use other useful resources.</label></div>\n  </div><div class=\"q-card ielts-listening-question-item\" id=\"lq-card-29\"><strong class=\"ielts-listening-question-number\">29</strong>\n    <div class=\"q-row\">\n      <span class=\"q-pill\">29</span>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What kind of help does Professor Smith think students should get?</div>\n      \n    </div>\n    <div class=\"options\"><label class=\"option\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"practice_7_29\" value=\"A\" id=\"practice_7_29_A\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 29: A\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span>classmates’ help</label><label class=\"option\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"practice_7_29\" value=\"B\" id=\"practice_7_29_B\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 29: B\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span>online help</label><label class=\"option\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"practice_7_29\" value=\"C\" id=\"practice_7_29_C\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 29: C\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span>teachers’ help</label></div>\n  </div><div class=\"q-card ielts-listening-question-item\" id=\"lq-card-30\"><strong class=\"ielts-listening-question-number\">30</strong>\n    <div class=\"q-row\">\n      <span class=\"q-pill\">30</span>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What is Professor Smith’s view on the purpose of introducing computers in school?</div>\n      \n    </div>\n    <div class=\"options\"><label class=\"option\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"practice_7_30\" value=\"A\" id=\"practice_7_30_A\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 30: A\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">A</span>for computer companies to sell computers more easily</label><label class=\"option\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"practice_7_30\" value=\"B\" id=\"practice_7_30_B\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 30: B\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">B</span>for cutting other fees</label><label class=\"option\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"practice_7_30\" value=\"C\" id=\"practice_7_30_C\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-label=\"Question 30: C\"><span class=\"opt-letter\">C</span>a simple way to make a profit</label></div>\n  </div>\n  </div>",
